uld not be until 1960 that women got a second Olympic event, " [:a {:href "/results/90185"} "team foil"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 1924 fencing events were contested at the " [:a {:href "/venues/277"} "Stade d’Escrime de Colombes"] " (épée and sabre) and the " [:a {:href "/venues/266"} "Vélodrome d’Hiver"] " (foil). France was the leading nation, winning three gold medals and six medals in all, although both Belgium and Hungary won four medals. Italy, normally a fencing power, struggled, winning " [:a {:href "/results/76478"} "team sabre"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/75902"} "a lone bronze medal"] " as its only two medals. Some of this was due to their team withdrawing after a protest in the " [:a {:href "/results/75460"} "team foil"] ". The drama of the 1924 Olympic fencing actually continued after the Games ended, as two actual duels were fought several months later due to disputes over referee decisions during the Games."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/74111"} "Foil, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "1 –  4 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "49"] "\n" [:td {} "17"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/75460"} "Foil, Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "27 – 30 June 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "67"] "\n" [:td {} "12"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/74397"} "Épée, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 – 11 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "67"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/75902"} "Épée, Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "6 –  9 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "89"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/75162"} "Sabre, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Ol